# Test: an action confirmed while the estate changes is still sent
# VALIDATES: spec-fleet-ui-1 AC on confirmations with the closure review's
#            confirm dialog finding -- a refresh that arrives while the
#            confirm dialog is open waits until it closes, so the control the
#            dialog was opened from is the one the confirmation submits
# PREVENTS: a confirmed Cancel that vanishes in silence, because a refresh
#           replaced the control and the script clicked the detached copy
#
# Goal: prove a confirmation survives a live refresh of the region that
# holds its control.
# Method: the sample script runs on its own timer here (not held), stepping
# every five seconds, and each step makes regions of the page stale. The
# task T-2051 is running (sample/script.go scriptSteps ends it at step 9), so
# its side panel on the task list carries Cancel, a destructive action
# confirmed by typing the task's id. The test opens the dialog, then waits
# for the root's data-fleet-held, which fleet.js sets when a refresh waits
# for the dialog; then it types the id and confirms. The hub answers any
# cancel, accepted or refused, with a toast linking to the task, which is the
# proof the post was sent. Every wait is on state the page shows.

option=needs-build-tag:value=ze_fleet_ui_sample:state=present
option=timeout:value=90s
option=viewport:width=1600:height=1000

action=open:path=/fleet/tasks/?id=T-2051
expect=html:id=fleet-side-panel:contains=T-2051
expect=attribute:selector=html:name=data-fleet-stream:value=open

action=click:text=button "Cancel"
expect=html:id=fleet-confirm:contains=Cancel the task T-2051
expect=attribute:selector=html:name=data-fleet-held:value=true

action=fill:text=to confirm:value=T-2051
action=click:text=button "Confirm"
expect=html:id=fleet-toasts:contains=Open the task
expect=html:id=fleet-toasts:not-contains=data-fleet-confirm-lost
